dep: re-wrap one line of _copy_dep_lists (no code change)

Sub-series: C (use_reduce parser) - patch 3 of 3; applies to 3.0.83 with only the earlier patches of this sub-series.
Of these it needs 0008 only.
Ported to upstream 73646c35d: unchanged (line numbers only)

One line of _copy_dep_lists(), the helper that patch 0008 adds, is
re-wrapped so that the series ends byte-identical to the tested tree. No
code change, nothing to measure. With this patch the tree is the tested
Python tree (the s10 arm of the ladder run).

This hunk was part of patch 0025 of the 25-patch ladder
(config-trims-and-leftovers). It is a patch of its own because it is the
only line of 0025 that needs another patch (0008), which would have tied
the leftovers to sub-series C.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20..21; cut out of its
former patch on 2026-11-21 without changing a line of code. Not a
human-written change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on
six states of one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the
same merge list in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts
and the same package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
